<title>SOUTH AFRICA: Western Deep Q1 available profit slumps.</title>
<headline>Western Deep Q1 available profit slumps.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-04-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Quarter to end-March versus preceding quarter</p>
<p>			(million rand unless stated)</p>
<p>    Available profit			  35.6 vs 66.1</p>
<p>    Capital spending			  25.5 vs 41.9</p>
<p>    Gold output (kg)			 7,770 vs 9,178</p>
<p>    Tonnes milled/treated	    1,183,000 vs 1,301,000</p>
<p>    Yield (gram/t)			    6.57 vs 7.05</p>
<p>    Cost (rand/kg)			  46,973 vs 40,683</p>
<p>    Revenue (rand/kg)		     52,541 vs 55,774</p>
<p>Full name: Western Deep Levels Ltd, managed by Anglo American Corp of South Africa Ltd</p>
<p>NOTE - The company said Western Deep was on track to attain its forecast gold production of 36 tonnes in 1997.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
</text>
